{
  "is_sufficient": false,
  "knowledge_gaps": [
    "Uniform aggregation does not isolate input dependence from learned depth preferences. Add a jointly trained, input-independent softmax depth-weight control as a separate single-model trial.",
    "Every softmax weight depends on all depth logits through its denominator. Deep historical context can therefore affect shallow-feature weights; favoring shallow depths does not establish exclusion of older history.",
    "Additional shared LayerNorm and intermediate-depth supervision alter normalization and gradient paths. The controls must distinguish these effects from adaptive context selection.",
    "Reproduction remains incomplete: concrete baseline settings, capacity-control architecture, compute allocation, validation schedule, and checkpoint-selection rules are unspecified. These require host-supplied implementation details rather than web research.",
    "Gate entropy and variability cannot establish useful adaptation or intent recognition. Test whether replacing dynamic weights with fixed weights changes deployed scores, while distinguishing inference perturbations from retrained controls.",
    "Originality 3 is plausible, but closer aggregation precedents are missing. Potential 7 remains speculative, and difficulty 3 understates diagnostic adaptation, memory overhead, controlled comparisons, and predictor export.",
    "Repeated selection on 800 validation users risks validation overfitting. Prespecify trial order and selection rules, log every validation query, and avoid treating small HR@10 changes as established improvements."
  ],
  "follow_up_queries": [
    {
      "reason": "Identify closer precedents and establish whether position-dependent aggregation contributes beyond established layer weighting.",
      "query": "What methods in sequential recommendation and causal convolutional networks learn input-dependent softmax aggregation over intermediate residual layers? Compare Jumping Knowledge Networks, ELMo scalar layer mixing, and dynamic layer aggregation, including learned static-weight and uniform-weight ablations."
    },
    {
      "reason": "Clarify the mechanism and prevent interpreting shallow gate weights as evidence that older context has been excluded.",
      "query": "For a causal dilated residual network with h_t = sum_d softmax(a_1,t,...,a_D,t)_d z_d,t, where each a_d,t depends on its depth representation z_d,t, how does the shared softmax denominator transmit long-context dependencies into shallow-depth weights? What dependency or intervention analyses distinguish depth selection from historical-context exclusion?"
    },
    {
      "reason": "Improve the experimental controls and assess whether reported gains could arise from normalization or optimization changes.",
      "query": "In learned aggregation of intermediate residual-network features, how do per-layer LayerNorm, shared affine normalization, and direct gradient paths affect optimization and feature scale? What ablations distinguish dynamic gating from static learned layer weights, normalization-only changes, and parameter-matched final-layer capacity?"
    }
  ]
}
